{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "id": "msg_011Ch1mhDCmyyzeiXbpP5HtP", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "I signed off after filing one bug and finding nothing else in the areas I covered. My confidence is moderate (0.6). I didn't test rotation, other note-type operations, or delete/undo flows.\n\n**Bug filed (confirmed by the developer):** In the \"Reposition new cards\" dialog in the card browser, the range hint reads \"Queue top: 1\" and \"Queue top: 7\". The second line should say \"Queue bottom\".\n\n**Checked, no problems found:**\n- **Deck retitling:** Renaming to a name that already exists is blocked with \"Name already exists\", including a different-case \"spanish\" and the subdeck path \"French::Verbs\".\n- **Expand/collapse arrows:** Both the expand and collapse arrows worked on the French deck once it had a subdeck.\n- **Field reorder:** Reordering fields kept the correct order immediately. It was still correct after leaving and reopening the note type, including a 3-field case.\n- **Card editing:** Editing the bonjour card's Back field and saving worked.\n- **Tag search:** Searching `tag:verb` returned only comer.\n\n**Test changes left in the data:**\n- A new French::Verbs subdeck.\n- An \"Extra\" field on \"Basic (and reversed card)\", now in the middle position after the reorder.\n- The Basic note type's fields now have Front first. I moved them twice and ended in the original order.\n- The bonjour card's Back field now reads \"hi there\" instead of \"hello\"."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 313, "cache_read_input_tokens": 45592, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 313}, "output_tokens": 478, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "